{
  "case_id": "2009-08-728",
  "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 12:59 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mark T. Stancil",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Pretrial motion preparation time is not automatically excluded under Section 3161(h)(1) of the Speedy Trial Act. Such delays are subject to exclusion only on a case-by-case basis under (h)(7)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: That would allow the prosecutor's time to be excluded, right? On your theory that it starts -- the trigger is the filing of the motion, and it ends when the motion is disposed of."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mark T. Stancil",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government acknowledges that courts treat pretrial motion delays under either (h)(1) or (h)(7), and more specifically (h)7)(B)(iv), which specifically speaks in terms of preparation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But -- it would seem to me that if a defense attorney comes to a court and says, I need an adjournment, and the Court says, you can have it, isn't that implicitly a proceeding in which the court is saying there is a need for this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STANCIL: I don't -- that sounds a lot like a prospective waiver of speedy trial, which is -- this court rejected in Zedner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Wait a minute. If a defense attorney comes in to you and says -- I'm a district court judge -- I need time to prepare; granted, I am excluding time under (7)(A). You are saying that is insufficient?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "district court judge: Defendant is arraigned; you have 21 days to file motions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Is -- is there any indication in the circuits that follow what seems to be the majority rule -- that is that the clock is stopped during preparation time -- that there have been excessive delays, in comparison to the -- what is it, two circuits who go the other way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STANCIL: The consequence -- ruling for the government would mean that any time a defendant needs any extra time, or -- or we would say either side needs any extra time, the clock stops."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "pretrial motions is automatically excluded from the Speedy Trial Act deadline for commencing trial. For three reasons, that time falls under section 3161(h)(1) which excludes delay resulting from other proceedings concerning the defendant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Could I ask a specific date question? Am I right that you would exclude the time from September 7th to October 4th?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROBERTS: Well, section -- Section (h)(1), Your Honor, expressly states that it excludes delays, including, but not limited, to the listed delays, so no negative inference arises from the fact that the listed examples don't specifically address delays resulting from the grant of additional motions preparation time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But that doesn't answer my point. Without a requirement that the judge actually has to make a finding in the interest of justice, once the defense attorney comes in and says, I want a month, and isn't the judge required to give him the month because it's automatically excludable? What, otherwise, forces the judge to look at the request and say, no; is it really in the interest of justice for me to give you that month?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So what -- so what additional requirements are we imposing on the judge that the statute itself doesn't command?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: If the judge always has to listen to the reason, weigh it, determine whether or not it is in fact in the interest of justice or not, how much more burden are we putting on a judge than to say, look, you are right, you need a month; I will exclude it under (7)(H)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Is that a normal course of practice? I've never quite heard of other --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But then the Court's view a decision or statement that no motions are going to be filed as a request for a waiver of that obligation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Can I ask you about the language of (h)(1)? Do you think it's -- do you think it's proper to consider a period of delay that precedes the filing of the motion? That is, a period of delay in order to prepare the motion, as a delay resulting from a proceeding that has not yet occurred?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: The grant of the motion is the proceeding?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mark T. Stancil (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The fall on that is evident by looking at subparagraph (h), which automatically excludes up to 30 days during which a matter is under advisement by the district court. If the government's reasoning is correct, subparagraph (h) just does not address or contains -- or suggests no negative inference on whether the 31st day of a matter being under advisement is automatically excludable under (h)(1)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mark T. Stancil (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.91,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0002-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, if you think there is any uncertainty as to what a proceeding is, well, look at how the enumerated subparagraphs that follow, what do they describe. One specifically addresses pretrial motions. It has a starting point and it has an end point. That's the end of this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mark T. Stancil (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0002-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In fact, with respect to defense requests specifically, it was not lost on Congress how to -- how to treat government counsel and defense counsel differently. In (h)(7)(C), which is about the end of justice exclusion, it specifies that the government cannot get an end of justice exclusion based on its inability to exercise due diligence in obtaining a witness or preparing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "None of the others do. So I would say right there, Congress doesn't want the judge to have it for more than 30 days. Congress doesn't say a word in any of the others that says anything about preparation time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "QED, their argument is literal and there is no policy against it. That's what they said."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Counsel, is your friend correct that the issue of the proper calculation is not before us?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-728",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c9dafb32d72eaf493e03911e46aa9096133e4b83b182d6afa796d339959f1ecb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c9dafb32d72e-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 2:01 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
